<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/medical">Medical</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">Medical MEMS &amp; Sensors</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Medical products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/hearing-aid-assembly"><span class="abbr">HA</span><span class="label">Hearing Aid Assembly</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/medical/mems-sensors"><span class="abbr">MS</span><span class="label">Medical MEMS &amp; Sensors</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/pcba"><span class="abbr">PB</span><span class="label">Medical PCBA</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/wireless-charging"><span class="abbr">WC</span><span class="label">Wireless Charging</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the device does and the regulatory route it follows and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Medical &middot; Medical MEMS &amp; Sensors</div><h1 class="mk-h1">MEMS and sensor assembly for medical devices</h1><p class="mk-lede">A MEMS die is sensitive to the package around it: die attach that cures under stress, or a cavity that closes unevenly, shows up later as drift in the sensor rather than as a visible assembly defect. Hana assembles air-flow, pressure and gas sensors for medical devices using low-stress die attach into cavity and sealed packages, with functional test on gas and MEMS rigs held in-house.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-mems-sensors" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ Medical MEMS &amp; Sensors &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-mems-sensors" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">The work runs under an ISO 13485 quality system with documented process control and traceability, because a sensor built into an inhaler, a respiratory device or a drug-delivery device is part of a regulated assembly. Sensor and MEMS assembly has been a Hana capability for years, alongside our IC packaging work.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Air-flow and pressure sensor assemblies</span></div><div class="desc">the MEMS and sensor assemblies used in inhalers, respiratory and drug-delivery devices, packaged and functionally tested.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Gas sensor assemblies</span></div><div class="desc">CO2, CH4 and R32 gas sensing assemblies built on the same sensor lines.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Cavity and sealed packaging</span></div><div class="desc">low-stress die attach into cavity and sealed package formats, where the die must not be loaded by its own package.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Functional test and traceability</span></div><div class="desc">gas and MEMS test rigs in-house, with material, unit and product traceability recorded through the build.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Process depth sits on the capability page: MEMS &amp; Sensor Assembly owns the wider sensor packaging range these builds draw on, including the clear and film-assist mold formats used where a device has to see out.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/microelectronic-assembly/mems-sensor-assembly">Explore MEMS &amp; Sensor Assembly <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Low-stress die attach and the package around it</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">The controlling variables in a medical sensor build are mechanical, not electrical. Hana works to that: attach materials and profiles selected to keep stress off the die, cavity and sealed package formats chosen with the sensing element in mind, and handling controlled through the line. Assemblies are then verified on gas and MEMS test rigs on our own floor rather than sampled downstream. Because the same site also runs IC packaging and test, a sensor program can draw on wafer-level handling and package assembly inside one company. For the wider optical and MEMS process set, see <a href="/markets/optical-sensors/mems-sensors">Optical &amp; Sensors</a>.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ayutthaya"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div><div class="note">medical MEMS and sensor assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">medical device assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">dedicated medical lines</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What medical sensor applications can Hana serve?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Air-flow and pressure sensing assemblies for inhalers, respiratory and drug-delivery devices, and gas sensing assemblies including CO2, CH4 and R32. The applicable format and test set are confirmed with our team per program.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Why does packaging stress matter in medical sensor assembly?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">A MEMS element responds to mechanical load, so stress introduced by die attach or by the package itself can appear as sensor drift rather than as an assembly fault. Hana uses low-stress die attach and cavity or sealed formats to keep that load off the die, and verifies the result on functional test.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How does traceability work on a medical sensor line?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Material, unit and product traceability is recorded as the assembly is built, under documented process control and change control — so a given sensor can be tied back to its materials, its line and its build record.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/medical" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Medical market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your medical sensor program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>
